HST Office: every Page Setup entry opens on the page tab, and the style organizer comes last in Sheets too.

- Writer: .uno:PageDialog without a page argument (ribbon button, the group launcher, the Format menu) opened on the
  tab the dialog was last closed on, so after a look at the organizer ("Chung") the next Page Setup opened there.
  It now opens on "page" as Word's Page Setup does; callers that name a page (header, footer, columns, area)
  are unchanged. A new page style is still named on the organizer.
- Sheets: the page style dialog moves the organizer after Page, Header, Footer, Sheet, Borders and Background
  (SfxStyleDialogController::HstMoveOrganizerToEnd, as Writer's page dialog), and opens on the page tab unless a
  new style is being named. Cell style dialogs keep the organizer first.

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
Test: tests/runtime/check-dialogs-writer.py page-setup; tests/runtime/check-dialogs-sheets.py page-setup
---
--- a/sw/source/uibase/shells/basesh.cxx
